# Migrations are forward-only

Named `NNN_description.sql`, applied in ascending numeric order, each inside its
own transaction.

- **Never write a down-migration.** A bad migration is corrected by a new
  migration. Rolling a schema backwards under a database holding real trade
  history is more dangerous than the defect being fixed.
- **Never edit a migration that has been applied anywhere.** Add a new one.
- Money columns are `TEXT`, never `REAL`. Timestamps are `TEXT` ISO-8601 UTC.
- Schema changes must be reflected in `technical-spec.md` §5 in the same change.
